  detailed_description: 'A356 is the most widely used aluminum casting alloy worldwide, with a hypoeutectic Al-7Si-0.3Mg composition. The microstructure features primary aluminum dendrites, Al-Si eutectic, and Mg2Si precipitates in the T6 condition. Silicon modification level and dendrite arm spacing are critical quality metrics. Commonly examined for foundry quality control, failure analysis, and heat treatment verification.',
  status: 'published',
