  detailed_description: 'A380 is the most widely used aluminum die-casting alloy, representing roughly 80-85% of aluminum die casting production. The Al-8.5Si-3.5Cu composition features primary aluminum dendrites, Al-Si eutectic, and Al2Cu (theta) intermetallic phase. Die castings typically contain gas and shrinkage porosity that are important features to preserve during preparation. Commonly examined for die casting quality control and failure analysis.',
