  typical_uses: '[Nuclear fuel rod cladding (Zircaloy),Chemical reactor vessels,Surgical implants,Heat exchangers,Pump impellers]',
  detailed_description: 'Zirconium is a moderately hard refractory metal with HCP crystal structure. PYROPHORIC in fine particle form; all debris must be kept wet. Chemically similar to hafnium but much lighter. Critical nuclear material for fuel cladding (as Zircaloy alloys). Polarized light microscopy is particularly valuable for grain structure analysis. Hydride platelets are a key degradation feature in nuclear applications.',
